WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.294 --> 00:00:03.859
The wheels of the cart continued to sink in the muddy alley.

2
00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:10.372
The old man, Fauchelevent, was still trapped under the wheels, and Mayor Madeleine was struggling to lift the cart.

3
00:00:10.373 --> 00:00:13.396
Everyone in the crowd was breathless with suspense.

4
00:00:13.397 --> 00:00:19.706
And then the cart began to rise slowly, its wheels coming half out of the ruts.

5
00:00:19.707 --> 00:00:22.676
"Help! Quickly!" cried Madeleine.

6
00:00:22.677 --> 00:00:27.356
Inspired by Madeleine's amazing strength, ten men rushed forward.

7
00:00:27.357 --> 00:00:31.776
Together they lifted the cart, and Fauchelevent was saved!

8
00:00:31.777 --> 00:00:34.433
Everyone was weeping with relief now.

9
00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:40.681
The mayor stood up, pale and dripping with sweat. His clothes were torn and covered with mud.

10
00:00:40.682 --> 00:00:46.943
He looked up and saw Javert, the police inspector, staring at him, but that didn't disturb him.

11
00:00:46.944 --> 00:00:51.016
Fauchelevent had broken his knee and was in need of medical care.

12
00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:58.587
Madeleine had established an infirmary for his factory workers in his home, so that is where Fauchelevent was taken.

13
00:00:58.588 --> 00:01:04.000
When the old man woke up the next morning, he found money on the bedside table.

14
00:01:04.001 --> 00:01:09.712
There was also a note from Mayor Madeleine, saying that he had purchased Fauchelevent's cart and horse.

15
00:01:09.713 --> 00:01:15.151
The cart was broken and the horse was dead, so they were of no use to anyone.

16
00:01:15.152 --> 00:01:19.484
Buying them was not the only kind thing that the mayor did for Fauchelevent.

17
00:01:19.485 --> 00:01:23.633
After Fauchelevent got well, he had difficulty finding work.

18
00:01:23.634 --> 00:01:28.389
The mayor found a job for him as a gardener at a convent in Paris.

19
00:01:28.390 --> 00:01:32.288
Meanwhile Javert continued to be suspicious of the mayor.

20
00:01:32.289 --> 00:01:38.056
He was always respectful when he encountered Madeleine, but he avoided the man as much as possible.

21
00:01:38.057 --> 00:01:43.310
Life went on for Javert and the other inhabitants of this small French city.

22
00:01:43.311 --> 00:01:48.635
For one young woman named Fantine, the city was about to become her home again.

23
00:01:48.636 --> 00:01:53.714
At this moment Fantine was entering the town of Montfermeil near Paris.

24
00:01:53.715 --> 00:01:58.111
She was carrying her daughter, Cosette, and a heavy carpetbag.

25
00:01:58.112 --> 00:02:04.040
Cosette, who was sleeping in her mother's arms, was the prettiest little girl that you could imagine.

26
00:02:04.041 --> 00:02:09.865
She was almost three years old, and her clothes were trimmed with ribbons and lace.

27
00:02:09.866 --> 00:02:16.119
In contrast, Fantine had the appearance of a working woman seeking to return to the life of a peasant.

28
00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:22.444
Her clothes were drab and plain. Her face was pale, and she looked weary and sick.

29
00:02:22.445 --> 00:02:31.254
In Paris, Fantine had lived a gay life. She was charming and beautiful, renowned for her thick blond hair and straight white teeth.

30
00:02:31.255 --> 00:02:35.341
But hard times fell upon her after she met a young man.

31
00:02:35.342 --> 00:02:43.087
Fantine thought they were in love—until he abandoned her. Soon afterward she discovered that she was pregnant.

32
00:02:43.088 --> 00:02:46.479
For a while Fantine managed to take care of her daughter.

33
00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:52.738
She stopped wearing the latest fashions and used the trimmings from her old clothes to decorate those of Cosette.

34
00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:59.079
But now at the age of 22, Fantine was desperate because she was running out of money.

35
00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:06.159
She began to think of returning to the city where she had grown up. Perhaps someone would remember her and give her work.

36
00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:12.722
So she sold everything she owned. When all her debts were paid, she had only eighty francs left.

37
00:03:12.723 --> 00:03:18.143
She had nothing in the world except her child, and she was going to have to give up Cosette.

38
00:03:18.144 --> 00:03:24.730
Fantine's heart ached, but she knew that no one would hire a woman with an illegitimate child.

39
00:03:24.731 --> 00:03:30.460
As she trudged into the town of Montfermeil, she spotted a charming scene outside an inn.

40
00:03:30.461 --> 00:03:38.047
A mother was sitting on the stone steps watching her two daughters at play. One was a rosy blonde and the other a brunette.

41
00:03:38.048 --> 00:03:46.436
The younger girl appeared to be about 18 months old while her sister was a year older. Their mother was a brawny red-haired woman.

42
00:03:46.437 --> 00:03:51.198
"You have two pretty children, Madame," Fantine said to the woman.

43
00:03:51.199 --> 00:04:00.190
"Thank you. I'm Madame Thenardier and my husband is the innkeeper. Why don't you sit by me and rest for a while? What brings you here?"

44
00:04:00.191 --> 00:04:07.087
Fantine sat on the steps and began to tell her story, which she changed slightly to make it more appealing.

45
00:04:07.088 --> 00:04:10.947
She said that she was a working woman and that her husband had died.

46
00:04:10.948 --> 00:04:16.763
Unable to find work in Paris, she was on her way to her hometown to look for employment.

47
00:04:16.764 --> 00:04:23.754
"My daughter walked a little," said Fantine. "But then I had to carry her, and the little jewel fell asleep."

48
00:04:23.755 --> 00:04:31.976
With those words, she gave Cosette a big kiss, which woke up the child. Cosette opened her big blue eyes and looked around.

49
00:04:31.977 --> 00:04:36.659
Spying the other two girls, she wiggled out of her mother's arms and ran to them.

50
00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:41.238
While the three girls played together, the two mothers talked.

51
00:04:41.239 --> 00:04:44.958
"What is your child's name?" asked Madame Thenardier.

52
00:04:44.959 --> 00:04:48.246
"Cosette. She's almost three years old."

53
00:04:48.247 --> 00:04:52.966
"The same age as my older daughter, Eponine. My younger girl is Azelma.

54
00:04:52.967 --> 00:04:58.557
Look at the three of them playing so nicely together. You'd swear they were sisters."

55
00:04:58.558 --> 00:05:02.550
Hearing those words, Fantine suddenly thought of a solution to her problem.

56
00:05:02.551 --> 00:05:07.541
She seized Madame Thenardier's hand and said, "Will you keep my child for me?"

57
00:05:07.542 --> 00:05:11.120
Madame Thenardier looked surprised but she said nothing.

58
00:05:11.121 --> 00:05:16.382
"You see, I cannot take my child with me to the country," continued Fantine.

59
00:05:16.383 --> 00:05:24.382
"With a child, I wouldn't be able to find work. The sight of your little ones, so pretty and clean and happy, has overwhelmed me.

60
00:05:24.383 --> 00:05:28.699
I can tell that you're a good mother and that they'll be like three sisters.

61
00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:33.366
It won't be long until I can come back for Cosette. Please keep her for me?"

62
00:05:33.367 --> 00:05:36.804
"I must think it over," said Madame Thenardier.

63
00:05:36.806 --> 00:05:38.953
"I'll give you six francs a month."

64
00:05:38.954 --> 00:05:45.691
"Make it seven francs," said a man's voice from within the inn. "And six months paid in advance."

65
00:05:45.692 --> 00:05:52.676
"That's my husband," said Madame Thenardier. "Seven francs times six months would be forty-two francs."

66
00:05:52.677 --> 00:05:59.017
"Plus 15 francs for any additional expenses," said Monsieur Thenardier from the interior of the inn again.

67
00:05:59.018 --> 00:06:06.589
"I'll give you 57 francs," said Fantine. "I have eighty francs, so that will leave me enough to get to the country if I walk.

68
00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:10.851
I'll earn some money there, and as soon as I can, I'll come back for my little love."

69
00:06:10.852 --> 00:06:14.509
"Does the child have clothing?" asked Monsieur Thenardier.

70
00:06:14.510 --> 00:06:18.501
"Of course she does, the poor darling," said Fantine.

71
00:06:18.502 --> 00:06:25.993
"It's an extravagant wardrobe too, with clothes by the dozens and silk dresses like a lady. It's all in my carpetbag."

72
00:06:25.994 --> 00:06:30.239
"Then I think we can keep her," said Monsieur Thenardier.

73
00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:35.144
Fantine spent the night at the inn, and the next morning she left for the country.

74
00:06:35.145 --> 00:06:38.469
A neighbor of the Thenardiers saw her on the road.

75
00:06:38.470 --> 00:06:45.890
"I've just passed a woman crying as if her heart would break," he said when he stopped at the inn. "I wonder what was wrong."

76
00:06:45.891 --> 00:06:54.882
"I have no idea," said Monsieur Thenardier, touching the 57 francs in his pocket. He had a debt that was due that day.

77
00:06:54.883 --> 00:07:00.208
Fantine's money would give him enough to pay it and keep seven francs for himself.

